BT 1 0 0 1 0 55.6 Tm 13 TL /F2 9.4 Tf .101961 .101961 .101961 rg (A NOTE ON THE TEXT.) Tj /F4 9.4 Tf ( In John 10:30 the Greek word for one is ) Tj /F2 9.4 Tf (hen) Tj /F4 9.4 Tf (, the neuter form, not ) Tj /F2 9.4 Tf (heis) Tj /F4 9.4 Tf (, the masculine.) Tj T* (Taken alone, the neuter means one thing, one in nature and unity, and it does not by itself say one person. Others will) Tj T* -0.01153 Tw (point that out, and they are right about the grammar. This study does not rest on John 10:30 alone. It rests on John 14:9,) Tj T* 0 Tw (Isaiah 9:6, and Colossians 2:9 standing together with it. Notice how the crowd heard it: they took up stones because,) Tj T* (they said, \223you, being a man, make yourself Elohim\224 \(John 10:33\).) Tj T* ET
